{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, subprocess, ast\nr=json.loads(subprocess.check_output(['python3','/workspace/tools.py','resolve','run://r-001']))\nconfig=ast.literal_eval(next(n.value for n in ast.parse(open('candidate.py').read()).body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets)))\nvariants=[]\nfor mode,role in [('joint','candidate'),('marginal','control')]:\n variants.append(dict(name='action_gap_'+mode,file='action_gap_'+mode+'.py',role=role,config={**config,'action_gap_mode':mode},note='Prospective compact gap-by-directed-behavior-table study; no new performance measured. Exact whole run_zero incumbent retained, append identical bias-free64->16->1 residual with zero final weights, no optimizer/loss change. Both cells compute identical observed/product alternatives. Training and scoring are host-owned; local checks will be appended before submission.'))\nstudy={\n'id':'g1-compact-action-gap-association',\n'protocol_ref':r['required_study_protocol_ref'],\n'evidence_refs':['g1-r0018-local_all','g1-r0018-global_all','g1-r0019-pooled_observed','g1-r0019-pooled_marginal','g1-r0020-direct_lifted','g1-r0023-serial_observed','g1-r0023-serial_symmetric','g1-r0023-serial_zero','g1-r0024-run_observed','g1-r0024-run_composition','g1-r0024-run_zero','baseline-static','baseline-pooled','baseline-din'],\n'question':'Does compact association between elapsed gap and the directed source/destination behavior pair add useful information beyond the same per-impression gap and behavior-transition margins, on the unchanged visible history?',\n'hypothesis':'Observation: the actual direct gap branch pools action/target states away, while the transition branch retains action transitions without gap; timing and symmetric serial branches retain times without actions. Existing source can therefore alias histories that differ in which behavior transition has a short versus long gap. Hypothesis: a compact H[gap,source action,destination action] preserves useful behavior-specific pace without the 4096-dimensional target/equality context expansion of the unsuccessful local_all branch. This information-loss mechanism is testable; its predictive utility is unestablished. The failed run histogram is not retained as an active signal: whole incumbent run_mode=zero is fixed.',\n'nearest_work':[\n{'source_ref':'paper:din, source-text://paper:din lines232-283, content-sha256:5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2','verification':'read','difference':'DIN primary text motivates target-dependent pooled interests and warns that naive sequence models need not help. Our supplied baseline is field-adapted and softmax-normalized; this candidate instead appends a deterministic temporal/behavior count residual to the existing local model. No exact author reproduction or priority claim.'},\n{'source_ref':'paper:dmr, author README at 2c6e76804281954a3c969010a31712cd5054aca9, content-sha256:656c9e5eec79c9843e907a555ede2bf0a66a0db3515916af3d655080057c5a75 lines1-9','verification':'read','difference':'Author README verifies history category/brand/behavior rather than item identity. Publisher paper remains unavailable; no full-paper mechanism claim. New branch uses only available action and age columns, with complete-pair singleton support inherited unchanged.'},\n{'source_ref':'g1-r0018-local_all and g1-r0018-global_all; candidate.py _GapParentModel._gap_tables and _GapTimingParentModel._direct_gap_counts','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Earlier large gap/context/equality readout already contained this association and underperformed pooling (AUC0.629916 versus0.630158). This is a compact reparameterization and a narrower attribution test, not newly discovered information:64 gap/action-transition counts, no target-match or identity-equality channels; one exact raw-margin product replacement.'},\n{'source_ref':'g1-r0024-run_zero and supplied history_g1_r0024_run_zero.py SHA256 edf3eeec4c93925847da35fb5fc7ba05d737dda040344365d9076a86fb6a409c','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Preserve every incumbent representation, parameter and allocation order. Append1040 dense parameters only after parent initialization. New branch links actions and time rather than adding higher-order action-free run lengths. Broader temporal recommendation literature and global novelty remain unverified; empty registry searches do not establish absence.'}],\n'inherited_components':['Frozen causal prefixes, first-six-day training exposures, natural label prevalence,3 epochs,batch4096,Adam lr0.001,seed42 and host scorer.','All run_zero source classes and parameter initialization order, including grouped means,count/histogram summaries,identity/context/repeat/overlap readouts,chronological product transitions,direct/lifted pooled gaps,joint endpoint timing and symmetric gap serial readout.','Complete category/brand support, remove all timestamp ties, chronological sort and compaction; excluded events may be bridged. All histories limited to supplied128 events.','Bias-free small residual pattern and zero final weight initialization inherited from earlier local studies. No new optimizer, supervision, fields or history.'],\n'proposed_difference':'Append H[b,g,s,d] with4 inherited gap bins (<=60,<=3600,<=86400,>86400 seconds),4 source and4 destination actions on the exact supported adjacent subsequence. Joint input is log1p(H)/log129 flattened64. Matched control replaces raw H by H[g,:,:].sum * H[:,s,d].sum / total within EACH impression, preserving gap and directed-action-pair margins before transformation, then uses identical64->16->1 head. Both variants execute both alternatives and preserve parent source. No extra target-match state, equality channel, fitted statistics or new event enters the branch.',\n'predictions':['The raw table agrees with an independent scalar oracle and sums to max(n_supported-1,0); its gap and action-pair margins agree with inherited gap/transition counts. Product preserves these margins including empty cases.','A constructed same-parent witness has equal event/action counts,age buckets,action-transition margins,gap histograms,timing tables and directed serial-gap table, but different joint action-gap tables. Product features and whole-parent logits should agree within float tolerance. This demonstrates representation difference, not efficacy.','If association is useful, joint should improve full validation AUC over marginal under the same recipe; report Logloss,paired seed variation and cost too. Improvements only versus historical parent do not isolate association.','Exploratory host history/action slices and first512 diagnostics describe support. Long histories dominate (3026583/3234051 exposures), so inspect empty/short groups without claiming significance or new confirmatory bins.'],\n'falsifiers':['Oracle/conservation errors beyond float accumulation tolerance, nonfinite logits/diagnostics, changed parent source or changed information/optimizer boundary invalidate the implementation comparison.','Joint fails to improve marginal, or any difference reverses across paired seeds: no supported predictive benefit for this compact association. Marginal benefit alone supports added readout/margins, not association.','The witness fails to separate joint or preserve replacement/parent: the asserted aliasing argument is wrong and must be revised before host execution.','The smaller head does not improve measured quality/cost relative to existing references: no efficiency gain, even if an AUC increase occurs.'],\n'alternative_explanations':['Large context table failed because of capacity/optimization/sparsity, not because action-gap information is useless; compact reparameterization is a discriminating but nonexhaustive retry.','log1p of observed and fractional product tables changes norms,sparsity and transformed margins; matched raw margins/parameters do not remove this scale confound.','Single-seed checkpoint selection,validation reuse across25 rounds,host nondeterminism and training interaction can explain small AUC changes. No significance or global novelty claim.','Filtering tied/missing-field events and128-event censoring creates supported-subsequence gaps rather than raw-log adjacency; behavior-specific rates may reflect support selection.','Candidate-supplied diagnostics cover first512 impressions only; they cannot establish full validation mechanism prevalence or independent efficacy. Static snapshot as-of dates are undocumented.','A pair-conditioned gap count does not identify causal behavior effects; it can proxy overall engagement or activity.'],\n'contrasts':[\n{'parent_ref':'g1-r0024-run_zero','intervention':'action_gap_joint: empirical H[g,s,d] in appended residual.','control':'action_gap_marginal: per-impression product of raw gap and directed-action-transition margins, same64-coordinate head and execution. Historical run_zero is the exact inherited function/reference; a fresh zero-input training cell is omitted to reserve paired repeats, so parent comparisons are historical rather than freshly paired.','held_fixed':['all inherited class ASTs apart from renaming final parent class','all parent config values,information boundary,data,seed,epochs,optimizer and loss','parameter shapes and order,head initialization,compute both alternatives and log transform','timestamp support and four fixed gap bins'], 'remaining_confounds':['fractional raw tables yield different post-log scales/sparsity','representational association versus optimization induced by that association','fresh zero-input training control absent; historical parent is not a contemporaneous equal-execution comparison'], 'decision_if_supported':'Freeze exact sources/configs and the joint/marginal comparison suite before assessment; prioritize paired seeds43/44 of these two cells if actual ledger permits. Claim only provisional local association support until repeated.','decision_if_not_supported':'Retain failed/null candidate and prior run/large-context failures; keep incumbent if best supported. Do not grow another temporal branch from these same validation fluctuations without new evidence.'}],\n'cost_plan':{\n'estimate_ref':'g1-r0024-run_zero wall870.957s/train746.972s and run_observed863.157s. remaining_seconds6514.061 at entry,hard per-trial cap1760.932s; estimated_unit_seconds704.373 underestimates current model.','all_variants_counted':True,\n'attribution_reserve':'Two new full-recipe cells at provisional950s each=1900s, including diagnostics; identical1040-parameter heads (expected17255107 total). Existing exact parent supplies a historical no-new-branch anchor; fresh zero control omitted deliberately. All preparation,checks,failures and retries remain charged. No local training; no hidden calibration runs.',\n'assessment_reserve':'Provisionally3800s for two additional paired seeds43/44 on the selected joint/marginal suite (4 cells at950s), leaving814.061s for preparation/contingency at entry. Seeds42 already executed in open research may be reused only with matching source/config/protocol hashes. Reserve is an estimate, not extra authorization; actual host ledger and cap govern. Validation only; no closed test access. If costs exceed forecast, reduce documented repetitions rather than raise budget.',\n'stop_rule':'Submit only these two cells; no further architecture search planned within this budget. Stop on hard ledger/cap,integrity failure or no complete admissible unit fitting remaining budget. Never retry unknown execution state automatically. Freeze candidate/control hashes,config/checkpoints,seeds and host commands before validation repetition assessment; report omitted repeats and all failures.'}}\np={'study':study,'parent_trial':'g1-r0024-run_zero','variants':variants,'knowledge_assessments':[]}\nfor id,reason in [('taac2026-academic-1-craft','No measured propagation instability; reliability-conditioned transport is not used.'),('taac2026-academic-2-unidac','Behavior labels are not business domains; dual compressed/local path and domain exchange do not isolate this gap/action association.'),('taac2026-academic-3-unitokenformer','No learned token allocation,projection or gated decoding used; organizer-only detail is insufficient for local component attribution.'),('taac2026-industry-1-queryformer','No observed query-construction bottleneck; learned attention-generated query probes are not adopted.'),('taac2026-industry-2-unidot','Local residual-head lineage is inherited; no per-layer dot-product highway or field/sequence bus fusion is adopted.')]:\n p['knowledge_assessments'].append(dict(knowledge_id=id,decision='considered',rationale=reason+' Only authorized shared card inspected; latest knowledge-usage and null/negative run outcomes reviewed. Reported conversion-task/system results do not transfer automatically.',transformed_mechanism='None adopted from this card. New compact gap-by-action-pair association derives from local source aliasing and revisits a negative large-context trajectory.',variant_names=[],nearest_work_difference=study['proposed_difference'],falsifier='This study cannot verify/refute that external architecture without its own controlled implementation; no priority or transfer claim.'))\np['knowledge_assessments'] += [dict(knowledge_id='paper:din',decision='used',rationale='Inspected authorized exact primary text lines232-283, including pooled representation and local activation; source cautions against assuming sequence modeling helps.',transformed_mechanism='Retain local pooling lineage; add explicit deterministic elapsed-gap/behavior-transition representation and raw-margin replacement control.',variant_names=[v['name'] for v in variants],nearest_work_difference='Fixed64 temporal/behavior counts with small residual rather than learned target attention; source baseline i